WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.450
American Horror Story is probably the most
terrifying, unsettling, brutally violent,

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.529
and bloody show on TV.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:11.400
Here are some photos snapped on the sets of
the various seasons that should make for a

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.260
nice, calming visual salve after viewing even
the most disturbing episodes.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.970
Cinematic Satan-worshippers may be all about
bringing the reign of pure evil to Earth,

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.769
but they also enjoy a certain level of fanciness.

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:28.300
In American Horror Story: Apocalypse, the
wicked leaders of Outpost 3 hold a handful

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.940
of survivors essentially captive, but still
make sure they dress in nice clothes, drink

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.320
out of nice goblets, and enjoy the occasional
celebratory banquet or high-end party.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.530
It's just nice to be fancy, even after the
end of the world.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.830
Leslie Grossman, along with other members
of the Apocalypse cast, had apparently spent

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.360
a few too many hours filming one of these
party sequences.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.510
With costars Joan Collins and Evan Peters
looking on in amusement, Grossman got so punch

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:59.760
drunk and silly that she and her blonde fright
wig took a faceplant on the fine china.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.150
Denis O'Hare disappears into his roles.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:06.170
He's clearly one of those actors who does
everything he can to learn everything about

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.820
a character, both inside and out.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.770
He's played many memorable parts in several
American Horror Story iterations, including

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:19.170
severely burned philanderer Larry Harvey in
Murder House, mute witch school servant Spalding

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.810
in Coven, and on Hotel, a transgender hotel
clerk with a heartbreaking backstory named

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.969
Liz Taylor.

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:30.710
Having lived as a Kansas salesman who secretly
wore women's clothing on business trips, a

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:35.770
visit to the Hotel Cortez and a meeting with
Elizabeth inspired Liz to be true to herself

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.200
and take a stint working at the haunted hotel.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.639
"You see everything when the world doesn't
see you."

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:46.359
Not only did O'Hare have to dig deep to find
the motivations and executions for his complex

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:49.060
character, he had to prepare his body, too.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.499
He endured extensive makeup to get that bald
head and heavily made-up look, as well as

00:01:53.499 --> 00:01:55.420
regular facial hair trim sessions.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.299
Here he is preparing for a shooting day.

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:02.789
Obviously, recurring American Horror Story
cast member and frequent Emmy nominee Sarah

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:07.679
Paulson doesn't have two heads in real life
which means the effects wizards behind American

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:10.920
Horror Story: Freak Show had their work cut
out for them.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.439
In order for Paulson to play Bette and Dot
Tattler, two heads with unique personalities

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:20.060
who shared a body, it required a lot of special
effects, digital manipulation, and time.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:27.390
"We could have such a fantastic time singin'
and dancin' on our own tv show."

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:32.030
First, the crew took a mold of Paulson's real
head and used it to build a prosthetic head

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.930
that bears a striking resemblance to the actress.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.720
The head was then positioned differently,
depending on if Paulson was filming her lines

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.190
as Bette or Dot.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.350
Scenes took as long as 15 hours to shoot,
and then the footage went to the computers

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.769
to make the idea of a double Sarah Paulson
seem visually convincing.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:53.400
One of the most memorable and striking characters
in American Horror Story will always be Pepper,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.860
who appears in both the Asylum and Freak Show
seasons, first as an institutionalized patient

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.810
and then as a performer in an unsettling traveling
sideshow.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:08.599
There's been no shortage of stunning transformations
among the AHS cast, but Naomi Grossman is

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:13.209
almost completely unrecognizable when she's
not in her Pepper guise.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:17.650
That's because becoming the character involves
an elaborate physical transformation that

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.659
was well-documented.

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:22.879
In addition to three hours in a makeup chair
for every day she was needed on set, Grossman's

00:03:22.879 --> 00:03:27.980
preparation required fake teeth, a single
contact lens that both distorted her vision

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.359
and altered the appearance of her eye, as
well as a unique hairdo.

00:03:32.359 --> 00:03:37.209
For that, Grossman had to shave off most of
her hair which was step one in her precise

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:39.849
and perfect Pepper preparations.

